WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:02.410
INTRO:
When most people think of credit cards, they

00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:06.000
think of debt, high interest rates, and predatory
lending.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.970
This is not surprising when you consider that
on average, Americans carry of $6,194 worth

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:13.330
of credit card debt.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:17.800
So, from their perspective, credit cards have
always been this sort of boogey man that results

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:21.250
in them overextending themselves and them
paying the price for years.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:26.230
But, contrary to what Dave Ramsey says, credit
cards don’t have to be a bad thing.

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:30.850
Most credit cards offer cash back, rewards,
flexible return policies, fraud protection,

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:34.070
the ability to build your credit score, and
so much more.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:38.590
And if you use these cards correctly, you
can actually profit quite a bit.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:42.670
This is especially true with American Express
cards which operate on a fundamentally different

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:44.850
basis to traditional credit cards.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.670
Many Amex cards don’t even allow you to
carry a balance meaning that you have to pay

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:50.990
off your entire balance every month.

00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:55.370
This is because charging stupid high interest
rates is not Amex’s top prioirity.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:59.710
Instead, Amex makes most of their money from
charging merchants higher fees and charging

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:01.460
card holders an annual fee.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:05.309
When applying for credit cards, you may have
seen credit cards with fees in the hundreds

00:01:05.309 --> 00:01:08.970
of dollars, but those are just the cards that
are offered to us peasants.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:13.710
The highest tier most exclusive Amex card
is called the Centurion card also known as

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.100
the black card.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:19.640
This card is invite only and is only offered
to the biggest businessmen and celebrities

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:20.640
in the world.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:24.120
But, just because you’re invited doesn’t
mean you get card.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:28.370
You actually have to pay a $10,000 initiation
fee along with $5,000 every year that you

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:29.630
have the card.

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:34.850
But despite this insanely high fee, the Amex
Black is by far the most sought after card

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:35.860
in the world.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:40.810
So, why are people willing to pay so much
for a piece of plastic, or I guess metal,

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:44.400
and what do you even get from owning this
elite card?

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:50.820
AN URBAN LEGEND:
Before we get into the perks of the card itself,

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:54.880
I think we should take a look at the history
of the card because its quite unique.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:59.110
It’s not like Amex had an idea to create
this super elite card that came along with

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:00.550
first class services.

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:05.420
Rather, the origin of the black card can actually
be traced back to urban legends.

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:09.629
It all started in May of 1988 when the Wall
Street Journal ran a story theorizing the

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:12.450
existence of an exclusive black card.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:17.249
The publication didn’t make their sources
clear, but apparently, Amex had been experimenting

00:02:17.249 --> 00:02:22.189
with a VIP card that was only offered to their
wealthiest and must trustworthy clients.

00:02:22.189 --> 00:02:26.849
According to the Journal, less than 1000 customers
were offered this card and it was only available

00:02:26.849 --> 00:02:30.069
for a mere four years before Amex cancelled
the program.

00:02:30.069 --> 00:02:33.909
When the card was available though, the perks
were really just up to your imagination.

00:02:33.909 --> 00:02:37.090
Did you forget to book a reservation at a
fancy restaurant?

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:40.200
Well, just call Amex and they’ll take care
of it.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.309
Did you forget your jacket at your hotel room?

00:02:42.309 --> 00:02:45.389
Well, just call Amex and they’ll take care
of it.

00:02:45.389 --> 00:02:46.809
Did you get lost in the desert?

00:02:46.809 --> 00:02:51.069
Well, you know the drill, just call Amex and
they’ll take care of it.

00:02:51.069 --> 00:02:54.590
As you can see, the Amex black wasn’t a
card with set in stone benefits.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:03:01.439
It’s not like you get 8% back on gas and
10% back on groceries and 15% back on flights.

00:03:01.439 --> 00:03:03.930
In fact, you couldn’t even be charged on
the card directly.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:08.219
Rather, charges would be routed to your Amex
platinum, gold, or green accounts.

00:03:08.219 --> 00:03:13.049
So, the card more or less just gave you the
ability to call Amex and put in requests.

00:03:13.049 --> 00:03:17.019
But, all of this was just the Wall Street
Journal’s theories and speculation.

00:03:17.019 --> 00:03:21.290
The only proof they had in support of the
black card even existing was a statement from

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:25.690
an Amex spokesman named Lee Middleton. Lee
confirmed the existence of the black card

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:29.769
and claimed that it was only offered to customers
with a “substantial banking relationship”

00:03:29.769 --> 00:03:30.769
with Amex.

00:03:30.769 --> 00:03:34.760
Lee went onto claim that the program was indeed
cancelled because “It just wasn’t worth

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:35.980
keeping it up.”

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:40.129
Lee wrapped up his statement by suggesting
that the new Amex platinum card offered 95%

00:03:40.129 --> 00:03:44.379
of the services that the black card did, so
there was no reason to continue offering the

00:03:44.379 --> 00:03:45.629
black.

00:03:45.629 --> 00:03:50.029
Despite this final statement, many Wall Street
Journal readers wanted the black card anyway.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:54.059
And over the next several years, we saw more
and more stories covering the alleged perks

00:03:54.059 --> 00:03:55.059
of this card.

00:03:55.059 --> 00:04:00.069
Soon enough, the black card became an urban
legend amongst finance and business nerds.

00:04:00.069 --> 00:04:03.599
But the ironic part is that the card likely
never even existed.

00:04:03.599 --> 00:04:08.140
But, wait a minute, didn’t the spokesman
basically confirm all of the Wall Street Journal’s

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.140
speculation.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:12.879
Well, yes he did, but there’s also evidence
that he was lying.

00:04:12.879 --> 00:04:17.709
You see, in 1999, Amex would actually launch
the Centurion Card, and the director of Amex

00:04:17.709 --> 00:04:20.170
Europe, Doug Smith, would come clean about
it.

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:23.830
Doug said quote, “There had been rumors
going around that we had this ultra-exclusive

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.640
black card for elite customers.”

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:29.170
“It wasn’t true, but we decided to capitalize
on the idea anyway.”

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:33.770
So, it looks like Lee was just leaning into
speculation to create hype for the company,

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:36.430
and a story from Jerry Seinfeld would further
verify this.

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:40.250
If you’re not familiar with Jerry, he’s
an extremely famous comedian who was the face

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:41.710
of Amex in the early 1990s.

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:46.930
And during one of his shoots, a crew member
would ask Jerry if he had a black card.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:50.480
Unfamiliar with the card, Jerry would ask
what is the black card?

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:53.930
The crew member would reply that it was a
super exclusive card that was only issued

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:55.990
to three people in the world.

00:04:55.990 --> 00:05:00.060
Apparently, one was given to the sultan of
Brunei, one was given to the president of

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:04.300
Amex, and the crew member was speculating
that the 3rd one was given to Jerry.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:09.520
Jerry obviously didn’t have one so he would
put this rumor to rest, but as you would guess,

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:10.630
he was quite curious.

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:14.420
So, he called the president of Amex the next
day to ask about the Amex black and here’s

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:15.980
what the president replied.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:17.710
"It's just a rumor.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:19.070
It doesn't exist.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:20.500
But you know what?

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:21.510
It's not a bad idea."

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:26.460
So, it looks like Lee was indeed just hyping
up the company, but Amex would eventually

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:29.060
answer these urban legends by launching the
card for real.

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:35.610
PERKS:
Now that the Amex black is actually a real

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:40.140
thing, it comes with a slew of defined benefits
starting with elite status at hospitality

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:41.140
brands.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:45.490
The card comes with IHG Platinum Elite, Hilton
Honors Diamond, Marriot Bonvoy Gold, and Relais

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:46.490
&amp; Chateaux 5C.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:52.530
In terms of travel, you get Delta SkyMiles
Platinum Medallion status which includes priority

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:56.020
waitlisting, priority check in and boarding,
and courtesy upgrades.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:06:00.000
If you have this card though, waiting at the
airport probably wouldn’t be that bad anyway

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.590
because you get access to the global lounge
collection.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:07.840
This includes lounges that are branded Centurion,
Amex, Priority Pass, Escape, Delta Sky Club,

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.840
Plaza Premium, and Air Space.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:13.970
You also get an invitation to Hertz Platinum
status and Avis President’s club.

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:17.580
Aside from travel benefits, you get a bunch
of retail benefits as well.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:21.120
For example, you get to be part of the Centurion
Shopping Program.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:26.260
And you also get 1.5X membership points on
purchases over $5,000, but honestly, none

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:28.920
of these perks are really that special.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:33.210
The Amex Platinum card has most of the same
perks and it has better rewards as well.

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:38.520
For example, the Amex Platinum offers 5X membership
points on flights and prepaid hotels.

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:43.490
Now, it’s not like the Amex Platinum is
cheap given that it costs $695 per year.

00:06:43.490 --> 00:06:47.550
But, it’s just a fraction of the cost of
the Amex Black and it comes with all of the

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:48.550
same tangible benefits.

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:52.860
So, if you’re just looking to churn credit
cards and earn rewards, there’s abosoluetly

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:54.640
no reason to get the black.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:58.870
The only reason to get the black is if you’re
looking for VIP service and this is where

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.680
the black really shines.

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:04.800
And I think the best way to really understand
the caliber of the VIP service is by simply

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:06.350
looking at stories.

00:07:06.350 --> 00:07:08.650
Take Chinese billionaire Liu Yiqian for example.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:13.020
Liu is an avid art collector and often buys
paintings that are worth tens of millions

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:15.100
if not over a hundred million.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:18.470
But instead of writing a check or completing
a wire transfer to buy these paintings, Liu

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:20.310
likes to put it on his Amex card.

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:24.870
One time, he put a $36 million tea cup from
the Ming dynasty onto his Amex.

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:29.690
But, by far his most outrageous credit card
purchase was a $170 million painting.

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:33.980
This purchase alone would’ve earned him
170 million Amex membership points.

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:38.330
Depending on how he redeemed these points,
he could get $1.7 million to $3.4 million

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.560
worth of rewards thanks to this purchase.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:44.420
Not to mention, Amex allowed him to bypass
Chinese transfer laws.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:48.570
You see, China doesn’t allow its citizens
to transfer more than $50,000 out of the country

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:49.970
in any given year.

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:53.900
But, since Liu charged it on a credit card,
he technically wasn’t transferring any money

00:07:53.900 --> 00:07:57.240
out of China, he was just paying off his credit
card.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:00.650
I suspect that that the CCP wasn’t that
happy to hear about this purchase.

00:08:00.650 --> 00:08:04.960
Aside from approving crazy large purchases,
Amex also bends to basically any customer

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:07.670
desire as long as it’s not illegal of course.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:17.960
You could say they live by the motto: And
believe me, they get some ridiculous requests.

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:21.630
For example, this one Amex Black client was
staying on a private island when they ran

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:22.630
out of ice cubes.

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:26.270
Instead of getting more ice from their beach
house or just drinking the rest of their drink

00:08:26.270 --> 00:08:30.280
without ice, the client decided to call Amex
and ask for ice.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:34.800
And sure enough, Amex ended up flying out
a bag of ice to the client on a helicopter.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:38.649
This other client asked Amex to deliver flowers
to 8 girlfriends in 4 different states and

00:08:38.649 --> 00:08:39.969
3 different countries.

00:08:39.969 --> 00:08:42.069
And Amex of course ended up doing it.

00:08:42.069 --> 00:08:46.410
While there are some crazy stories of people
abusing the system like this, the vast majority

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:49.390
of cenutrion customers don’t actualy make
such requests.

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:52.550
More times than not, they just want their
entire travel experience to be taken care

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:53.550
of and streamlined.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:57.800
These guys don’t want to think about booking
flights and hotels and making restaurant reservations

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.810
and travel arrangements and so on.

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:03.379
They like the convenience of calling Amex
and telling them where they wanna go and what

00:09:03.379 --> 00:09:05.839
they wanna do and have Amex take care of the
rest.

00:09:05.839 --> 00:09:10.480
And given that many of these guys are extremely
frequent travelers, such a service is invaluable

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.519
to them.

00:09:11.519 --> 00:09:16.970
GETTING A CENTURION CARD:
Hearing all of that, I’m sure that getting

00:09:16.970 --> 00:09:20.920
an Amex centurion card is likely a goal for
some of you ambitious souls out there.

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:23.640
So, how exactly do you go about getting the
black card?

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:28.589
Well, at first glance, it might seem like
you have to be a billionaire or celebrity,

00:09:28.589 --> 00:09:31.139
but this is not actually true.

00:09:31.139 --> 00:09:34.930
Really, it just comes down to spending a lot
of money on Amex cards.

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:38.330
No one really knows what the threshold is
for Amex to consider you.

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:41.949
Some estimates say that you have to spend
$250,000 per year while others say that you

00:09:41.949 --> 00:09:43.600
have to spend a million per year.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:48.529
To be honest, I don’t think there is a threshold
per se, and each approval is likely given

00:09:48.529 --> 00:09:50.100
on case by case basis.

00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:53.850
For example, if you have some sort of notoriety
from being an actor or singer or something

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:57.930
like that, you can probably get approved with
lower spend because giving you the card would

00:09:57.930 --> 00:10:00.389
likely give Amex some exposure as well.

00:10:00.389 --> 00:10:04.199
But, if you’re a background businessman
that owns a couple of car dealerships or something,

00:10:04.199 --> 00:10:07.329
you probably have to have much higher spend
to get an invitation.

00:10:07.329 --> 00:10:11.860
Regardless of your status though, if you consistently
spend a boat load of money as in half a million

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:15.809
or more per year, chances are, you’ll get
an invitation.

00:10:15.809 --> 00:10:19.009
Something to keep in mind though is that if
you’re just trying to get the card for status

00:10:19.009 --> 00:10:21.980
or clout though, the card is probably not
for you.

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:25.880
The true purpose of the card is to getting
valuable concierge services, and if these

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:29.480
services don’t really apply to you, you’re
just burning money on the annual fee for a

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:30.480
bit of attention.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.279
Not to mention, the type of attention that
you get from owning such a card is not exactly

00:10:33.279 --> 00:10:35.350
the type of attention that you want.

00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:39.059
Sure, it might be cool amongst your friends
and family and business acquaintances who

00:10:39.059 --> 00:10:40.730
will be impressed and happy for you.

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:44.249
But, whipping out such a card at Walmart is
likely not the best idea.

00:10:44.249 --> 00:10:48.509
So, just make sure you’re getting the card
for the right reasons, but that’s just what

00:10:48.509 --> 00:10:49.509
I think.

00:10:49.509 --> 00:10:50.940
Would you guys get a Centurion card?

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:51.940
Comment that down below.

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:55.999
Also, drop a like if you’re a fan of using
credit cards the right way.

